            { question_text: "How does Docker layer caching accelerate CI/CD pipelines for AI Docker images?", scenario_context: "Your CI/CD pipeline rebuilds your ML service Docker image from scratch in 8 minutes on every commit.", options: ["Docker caching requires special CI/CD configuration", "Copying requirements.txt and installing dependencies before application code allows Docker to cache the dependency layer — rebuilding only changed layers on code changes", "Docker caching only works for the base image layer", "Docker caching is not available in CI/CD environments"], correct_answer_index: 1, explanation: "Docker builds layer by layer and caches unchanged layers. By installing dependencies (rarely changed) before copying application code (frequently changed), only the code layer rebuilds on code commits — reducing an 8-minute image build to 30 seconds for most code changes." }
